<h2>A bit about <%= @show.name %></h2>
<p>Damon Castillo is a songwriter, producer and mixer whose eclectic, jazz-informed rock, funk and soul paint a sun-bleached portrait of life and love in the Golden State.</p>

<p>Born in Santa Maria, California, Damon headed east after high school to study jazz at — where else — Berklee. He then returned west and settled in San Luis Obispo, where he leads the Damon Castillo Band. He also runs a studio, producing and mixing records for other artists. His music has turned up in campaigns for Target, Starbucks, Miller Lite and MTV, so there’s a chance you’ve heard Damon without knowing it.</p>

<p>Damon’s albums, including <cite>Mess of Me</cite>, <cite>Laurel Lane</cite>, <cite>Live at the Mission</cite> and <cite>Revolving Door</cite>, feature Grammy winners Ross Hogarth and F. Reid Shippen. He has a publishing deal with Warner Chappell and has shared the stage with Chicago, John Scofield, The Temptations, Train and Chris Isaak.</p>

<p>Get ready for the show with his recent singles “Say It Now,” “Blue Sky” and “My Kind of Jam.”</p>

<p><%= link_to "Spend #{@show.day_of_week} evening with #{@show.name}", @rsvp_url_yes %>.</p>

<p><br/>Paul</p>

<p>P.S. If you have moved or don’t want to receive house concert invites, <%= link_to "instantly unsubscribe", @unsub_url %>.</p>

